{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And when a man acts presumptuously.</b> Why is this said? For since it is said ״מַכֵּה אִישׁ״ etc., I would hear even a gentile, and a doctor who caused death, and an agent of the court who caused death with forty lashes, and a father striking his son, and a teacher disciplining his student, and the inadvertent — therefore Scripture says: ״וְכִי יָזִד״ — and not inadvertent; ״עַל רֵעֵהוּ״ — and not a gentile; ״לְהָרְגוֹ בְעָרְמָה״ — and not an agent of the court, and not the doctor, and not one disciplining his son and his student — for even though they act with intent, they do not act with cunning (Mekhilta)." "<b>From My altar.</b> If he was a kohen and wants to perform the divine service — you take him to die (Yoma 5)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:32.403848594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}